    "version": 1,
    "kind": "certification",
    "proves": "Verify that the core Globular services are registered in etcd after cluster boot.\nRegistration in etcd means the service started, connected to etcd, and announced itself.\nThis is a proxy for service health \u2014 if a service crashes before registering, it won't appear.\n\nServices checked:\n  - cluster controller (control plane decisions)\n  - node agent (execution layer)\n  - workflow (state machine engine)\n  - cluster doctor (health analysis)\n  - authentication (JWT tokens)\n  - rbac (permission enforcement)\n  - dns (name resolution)\n\nThis test proves the stack is alive end-to-end, not just that containers are running.",
